WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.647
Column pruning means the engine may read only needed columns,

00:00:03.647 --> 00:00:07.797
especially with columnar formats such as Parquet and Delta.

00:00:07.797 --> 00:00:12.787
This is one reason SELECT star can be costly in large analytical work.

00:00:12.787 --> 00:00:19.492
It may be fine during exploration, but production transformations should choose needed columns deliberately.

00:00:19.492 --> 00:00:25.952
Partitions organize data so the engine can avoid reading files that cannot satisfy a filter.

00:00:25.952 --> 00:00:31.002
Good partition columns are commonly filtered and have manageable cardinality.

00:00:31.002 --> 00:00:34.942
Column pruning similarly avoids reading unused columns.

00:00:34.942 --> 00:00:40.009
Both optimizations reduce I/O before more expensive computation begins.
